# Everything listed here is excluded from the BUILD CONTEXT -- the set of files
# Docker uploads to the build engine before running the Dockerfile.
#
# Three reasons this file matters, in order of importance:
#
# 1. SECURITY. `COPY . .` copies whatever is in the context. Without this file
#    your `.env`, your `.git` history (which contains every secret ever
#    committed, even ones later deleted), and any stray *.pem would be baked
#    into the image. Anyone who can pull the image can extract them with
#    `docker history` or by simply running a shell in it.
#
# 2. SPEED. The whole context is transferred before the build starts. A .venv
#    directory is hundreds of megabytes of files the image will never use.
#
# 3. CACHE CORRECTNESS. Any change inside the context can invalidate the
#    `COPY . .` layer. If .pytest_cache is included, merely running the tests
#    busts your cache and forces a rebuild.

# --- Secrets: never, under any circumstances -----------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets.yaml
credentials.json
*.tfvars

# --- Git ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .git can be large AND holds the full history of every secret ever committed.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- Python build/runtime artefacts ---------------------------------------------
# .venv is built for macOS/arm64 on your laptop; the image builds its own for
# Linux. Copying it in would produce broken, mismatched binaries.
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info

# --- Test and lint artefacts ----------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov
tests

# --- Infrastructure: not needed to RUN the app ----------------------------------
# These describe how to deploy the image; they do not belong inside it.
terraform
k8s
monitoring
docs
.terraform
*.tfstate*

# --- Local databases ------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.sqlite3

# --- Editors and OS -------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.swp

# --- Docker's own files ---------------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
README.md
